Subject: [PATCH 1/4] marianos-azure-headless 1.10.0rc7: tests only (a
 listing's verdict from the products accounted for; the CSV contract)

Darren's review of R7 (2026-11-20): the coverage file reported Dog Food 27017 and Cat Treats
27022 DONE with no gap while 44 products of their counted pages had no record. These tests
are committed before the fix and hold 1.10.0rc6's code with OR-21 to OR-24 (021b23f):

- unit/test_route_audit_rc7.py: the audit of one listing and of a listing read through
  subdivisions (Cat Food 234/234 control; Dog Food page 7 and Cat Treats page 2 short;
  223 of 224; equal counts with a substituted UPC; overlapping subdivisions; an unbound
  brand reading; a page not bound to the store; an empty listing with and without the
  store's zero-result page; a repeated page; a changed total; carried, cross-listed,
  excluded and sponsored products kept apart).
- integration/test_route_audit_rc7.py: a counted product without a record (1 of 61, and a
  whole page) is INCOMPLETE in the node coverage, the coverage files, G3 and the export, and
  is never published, manually or automatically, the previous good dataset kept; the
  publication reads the coverage again whatever the recorded checks say; one lane and two
  lanes in either completion order keep the same UPC sets, memberships, hashes and export;
  a two-lane worker killed mid-run leaves every counted page whole and resume completes it;
  controls that pass before and after.
- unit/test_contract_csv_rc7.py: validate-export --file reads products.csv.
- c1_site.py: the kill helper passes the lane count.
