+"""Release 1.10.0rc7: a listing is complete only when the products its counted pages list are accounted for.
+
+Darren's review of the full run R7 (2026-11-20): the coverage file reported Dog Food 27017 and Cat Treats
+27022 DONE with no gap while 44 products of their counted pages had no record (OR-24); G3 read the cursor's
+own count (0.893 and 0.615, both below the 0.90 threshold, so R7 was refused). A smaller loss passes every
+threshold: one product of 61 is a coverage of 0.984, above the warning (0.98), and 1.10.0rc6 validated and
+published such a run.
+
+SYNTHETIC pages (``tests/listing_site.py``, the C1 site at Vernon Hills, Pickup) behind a local mock
+transport: no request leaves the process. A lost record is injected (``record_step`` leaves out the named
+cards: a counted page whose products are not kept, the class of OR-24). The publication target is each
+test's own throwaway database and folder. With ``PUBLICATION_EVIDENCE_DIR`` set, each test writes what it
+observed there.
+
+Tests named ``test_rc7_...`` fail on 1.10.0rc6 (``review-1.10.0rc6-20261117``); ``test_control_...`` pass on
+both. ``test_lanes_...`` compares two lanes with one on identical pages: in R7's order (a named product's page
+answered after the other lane's listing) it fails on 1.10.0rc6 (OR-24), in the other order it passes on both.
+The file loads on 1.10.0rc6 (it reads the coverage through what rc6 already has)."""
+
